## What was wrong

The endpoint modules (cart, invoice, customer, search) all build payloads with storage-style `snake_case` keys and delegate to `toWire` for translation — so the actual divergence was concentrated in the boundary helper, `src/wire.js`. `toCamel` only handled `snake_case`, not the `SCREAMING_SNAKE` variant its own doc comment promised:

- `toCamel('LINE_TOTAL')` returned `'LINETOTAL'` instead of `'lineTotal'`, so any upper-cased key (e.g. legacy CSV-origin fields) leaked onto the wire malformed.

## The fix

One change in `src/wire.js` — `toCamel` now splits on `_-` delimiters *and* existing camel boundaries, lowercases each word, then re-capitalizes leading words:

```js
export function toCamel(key) {
  return String(key)
    .replace(/[-_]+/g, ' ')
    .replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, '$1 $2')
    .split(' ')
    .filter(Boolean)
    .map((word, index) => {
      const lower = word.toLowerCase()
      return index === 0 ? lower : lower[0].toUpperCase() + lower.slice(1)
    })
    .join('')
}
```

Because every payload builder (`cartPayload`, `invoiceLine`, `customerPayload`, `productHit`, `facets`, …) funnels through `toWire` → `renameKeys`, this single fix cascades across all four endpoints, including the nested shapes: cart/invoice `lines`, the customer `defaultAddress`, search hits, and the facets envelope. Already-camelCase keys round-trip unchanged, and `toSnake`/`fromWire` are unaffected, so request bodies keep working.

